      "id": "179",
      "type": "writeup",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 179,
        "body_ja": "",
        "body": "<p>As we explored in our lesson about <span data-gp-id='112'>がる</span>, this verb can be used with adjectives, to express the way in which people are acting. However, it can also be partnered with the <span data-term='助動詞・じょどうし'>auxiliary verb</span> <span data-gp-id='59'>たい</span>, to form <span data-gp-id='124'>たがる</span>. This grammar construction is used when expressing that someone is acting like they 'want' to do something.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To use this structure, attach <span data-gp-id='59'>たい</span> to the ます stem form of any verb, then replace the い in <span data-gp-id='59'>たい</span> with <span data-gp-id='112'>がる</span>.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='180379'>\r\n<li data-study-question='180380'>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<section class='caution'><h4>Caution</h4>\r\n<p><span data-gp-id='124'>たがる</span> is in contrast to <span data-gp-id='101'>てほしい</span> which means 'to want someone to do (A)'. These differences will need to be practiced, and memorized.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'>\r\n<li data-study-question='183894'>\r\n<li data-study-question='183895'></ul>\r\n\r\n<p>This is also in contrast to the <span data-gp-id='24'>い-Adjective</span> 欲（ほ）しい 'to want (A)'. To describe that someone seems like they want something (rather than that they want to 'do' something), <span data-gp-id='112'>がる</span> will be paired with this adjective.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul class='writeup-examples--holder'><li data-study-question='183896'></ul></section>"
      }
    },
