    {
      "id": "210",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 210,
        "relationship_type": "synonym",
        "body": "The たい form expresses personal desires, such as 日本に行きたい ('I want to go to Japan'). がる, on the other hand, is a suffix that shows when someone else appears to want something, like 日本に行きたがっている ('They seem like they want to go to Japan'). The たい form is typically not used for expressing others' desires unless quoting the subject.",
        "first_relatable": {
